WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.968 --> 00:00:02.067
-I have a big announcement

00:00:02.067 --> 00:00:02.901
I have to make tonight.
-What's that?

00:00:02.901 --> 00:00:03.767
-This is a giant, giant deal.

00:00:03.767 --> 00:00:06.133
I'm very excited about this.

00:00:06.133 --> 00:00:09.501
So I've been working
on a holiday song, okay?

00:00:09.501 --> 00:00:10.701
[ Laughter ]

00:00:10.701 --> 00:00:12.734
[ Cheering and applause ]
A comedy song and...

00:00:12.734 --> 00:00:14.767
you work on it
and The Roots know

00:00:14.767 --> 00:00:16.501
is not easy to really --

00:00:16.501 --> 00:00:18.200
It's takes time
to write and produce

00:00:18.200 --> 00:00:20.334
and mix and do all stuff.

00:00:20.334 --> 00:00:21.934
So I've been working on this.

00:00:21.934 --> 00:00:23.567
I'm working on different songs.

00:00:23.567 --> 00:00:26.634
They're funny,
but then, I got one song --

00:00:26.634 --> 00:00:29.901
Because I'm in Electric Lady
Studios here in Manhattan.

00:00:29.901 --> 00:00:31.934
After the show, I go there
from like 7:00 to midnight

00:00:31.934 --> 00:00:33.934
and just hang out and just try
to write and things.

00:00:33.934 --> 00:00:35.067
So, you see people
in the building,

00:00:35.067 --> 00:00:36.734
who's there and stuff,
so they go,

00:00:36.734 --> 00:00:38.367
"Why don't you meet
with this producer?"

00:00:38.367 --> 00:00:41.200
A guy named Ido, and Aldi
are these two producers

00:00:41.200 --> 00:00:42.400
and they know how
to write music.

00:00:42.400 --> 00:00:44.534
So I get to these guys
and we write this song

00:00:44.534 --> 00:00:45.734
and I think it's something.

00:00:45.734 --> 00:00:46.567
-Mm-hmm.

00:00:46.567 --> 00:00:47.901
[ Laughter ]

00:00:47.901 --> 00:00:49.834
-I think
we could have something.

00:00:49.834 --> 00:00:51.100
-Whoa!
-I've never written a song

00:00:51.100 --> 00:00:52.701
where I go like,
"We got something."

00:00:52.701 --> 00:00:54.767
-Well.
-I go, "That's funny,"

00:00:54.767 --> 00:00:56.834
or whatever.
But this one, I go,

00:00:56.834 --> 00:00:58.501
"This is something."
[ Laughter ]

00:00:58.501 --> 00:01:01.634
So I go to the record label.

00:01:01.634 --> 00:01:03.567
I went
to Michele Anthony's house

00:01:03.567 --> 00:01:07.000
and Monte Lipman was there
and I played the song for them.

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:08.467
This is the heads of the label.

00:01:08.467 --> 00:01:09.801
I played the song.

00:01:09.801 --> 00:01:11.267
It's a demo.
I play it.

00:01:11.267 --> 00:01:13.100
Listen to it, loud.

00:01:13.100 --> 00:01:14.267
The kids are there.

00:01:14.267 --> 00:01:16.334
Song ends. Quiet.

00:01:16.334 --> 00:01:17.767
[ Laughter ]
No one says anything.

00:01:17.767 --> 00:01:19.467
-Oh.

00:01:19.467 --> 00:01:20.934
-Monte stands up.
He come over to me.

00:01:20.934 --> 00:01:22.801
He goes,

00:01:22.801 --> 00:01:23.501
"You got a hit."

00:01:23.501 --> 00:01:24.667
-Yeah!

00:01:24.667 --> 00:01:26.868
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:01:26.868 --> 00:01:29.367
-So you know Monte, right?
-Yeah.

00:01:29.367 --> 00:01:31.000
-So I go, "Now, what do we do?"

00:01:31.000 --> 00:01:32.767
Because it's, you know --

00:01:32.767 --> 00:01:33.968
so, anyways, I'm like,

00:01:33.968 --> 00:01:35.901
it's basically about like

00:01:35.901 --> 00:01:37.601
how last year was just rough
on everybody

00:01:37.601 --> 00:01:40.434
and, you know,
I wanted to say like, you know,

00:01:40.434 --> 00:01:42.033
it's going to get better.
It really is going

00:01:42.033 --> 00:01:43.467
to get better.
Trust me.

00:01:43.467 --> 00:01:45.534
And how can I portray that
and also think

00:01:45.534 --> 00:01:46.901
about what funny things happened

00:01:46.901 --> 00:01:49.300
while we were in lockdown,
you know.

00:01:49.300 --> 00:01:50.734
Putting Purell on everything

00:01:50.734 --> 00:01:52.000
[ Laughter ]
or, you know,

00:01:52.000 --> 00:01:55.267
going onto Zoom,
Zooming your grandpa,

00:01:55.267 --> 00:01:56.400
[ Laughter ]
you know, grandma

00:01:56.400 --> 00:01:59.901
and seeing where
the Wi-Fi works best.

00:01:59.901 --> 00:02:01.133
So we start writing the song.

00:02:01.133 --> 00:02:03.601
They go, "Well, our dream is
Ariana Grande

00:02:03.601 --> 00:02:04.467
to do the song with."

00:02:04.467 --> 00:02:05.934
I go, "Wow.
Good luck."

00:02:05.934 --> 00:02:07.400
[ Laughter ]
I mean, but whatever.

00:02:07.400 --> 00:02:08.601
She's the greatest.

00:02:08.601 --> 00:02:10.601
I mean, she's gorgeous.

00:02:10.601 --> 00:02:12.300
She can sing like an angel.

00:02:12.300 --> 00:02:14.501
She's funny.
We've had her --

00:02:14.501 --> 00:02:16.300
We've been friends
since "Late Night,"

00:02:16.300 --> 00:02:18.734
you know, Ariana Grande.
So I go, "Well, why not?

00:02:18.734 --> 00:02:20.601
Let's just go out to her
and see if she wants to do it."

00:02:20.601 --> 00:02:22.634
We go out to her.
We don't hear back.

00:02:22.634 --> 00:02:23.601
Okay, good. But whatever.

00:02:23.601 --> 00:02:24.634
[ Laughter ]
I know she's fine.

00:02:24.634 --> 00:02:25.767
I see her on "The Voice."
She's fine.

00:02:25.767 --> 00:02:28.334
[ Laughter ]

00:02:28.334 --> 00:02:29.767
I got a text from Ariana.

00:02:29.767 --> 00:02:32.167
"Jimmy, I love the song.
I'm in."

00:02:32.167 --> 00:02:32.868
-Oh.
-I mean, the song --

00:02:32.868 --> 00:02:34.133
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:02:34.133 --> 00:02:36.834
-Whoa!

00:02:36.834 --> 00:02:39.334
-So, now, I know this is --
-I want to hear this.

00:02:39.334 --> 00:02:41.000
-I know, I know. I got
to tell you the story, though.

00:02:41.000 --> 00:02:43.133
So it's great.
So like maybe two months ago,

00:02:43.133 --> 00:02:44.501
the song was nothing.

00:02:44.501 --> 00:02:45.834
It just wasn't going anywhere.
I didn't know --

00:02:45.834 --> 00:02:46.868
We didn't hear back
for anything.

00:02:46.868 --> 00:02:48.300
I go, "I guess it just
won't come out."

00:02:48.300 --> 00:02:50.734
It's just the way life works.
Okay.

00:02:50.734 --> 00:02:52.667
Ariana says, "I'm in.
I'm out in L.A.,

00:02:52.667 --> 00:02:53.934
doing 'That's My Jam.'"

00:02:53.934 --> 00:02:55.701
She goes, "I'm in. I'm recording
tomorrow at the studio."

00:02:55.701 --> 00:02:58.834
Records her track,
does backing vocals.

00:02:58.834 --> 00:03:00.634
My song sounds better
than it was.

00:03:00.634 --> 00:03:02.000
[ Laughter ]
-Whoa.

00:03:02.000 --> 00:03:03.234
-Whoo!
-It's unbelievable.

00:03:03.234 --> 00:03:04.601
I go, "This is unbelievable."

00:03:04.601 --> 00:03:06.534
She goes, "Who's going
to do the rap on the song?"

00:03:06.534 --> 00:03:08.501
Because, on the demo, I rapped.

00:03:08.501 --> 00:03:10.000
[ Laughter ]
I was hoping --

00:03:10.000 --> 00:03:11.334
-Hey, hey, hey, don't laugh!

00:03:11.334 --> 00:03:14.033
-I was hoping she'd say,
No, Jimmy, you can do the rap."

00:03:14.033 --> 00:03:15.901
[ Laughter ]

00:03:15.901 --> 00:03:19.767
She goes, "Maybe we should see
if Meg wants to do the rap."

00:03:19.767 --> 00:03:21.801
[ Audience ohs ]
I'm like, "Megan Thee Stallion?"

00:03:21.801 --> 00:03:23.133
She's like, "Yeah."

00:03:23.133 --> 00:03:24.367
I got to hang up the phone.

00:03:24.367 --> 00:03:26.267
[ Laughter ]
Hold on. It's like freaking out.

00:03:26.267 --> 00:03:27.701
So I'm getting sweats
and I'm freaking out.

00:03:27.701 --> 00:03:29.901
I go, "Now,
this is a real song."

00:03:29.901 --> 00:03:31.133
Text Megan Thee Stallion.

00:03:31.133 --> 00:03:32.868
Megan Thee Stallion goes,
I get to do a song

00:03:32.868 --> 00:03:34.634
with my besties
Ariana and Jimmy?

00:03:34.634 --> 00:03:36.400
I'm in.
When do we shoot the video?"

00:03:36.400 --> 00:03:38.701
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:03:38.701 --> 00:03:42.267
Dude, Quest, I didn't tell you
about it, though.

00:03:42.267 --> 00:03:44.133
Dude, this all happened
in like a month.

00:03:44.133 --> 00:03:45.267
-Okay.
-I didn't tell you this

00:03:45.267 --> 00:03:46.534
because I didn't want to --

00:03:46.534 --> 00:03:48.067
I mean, you got your own stuff.
Your, you know.

00:03:48.067 --> 00:03:49.667
-Ah, you know.
-Yeah, "Summer of Soul."

00:03:49.667 --> 00:03:51.200
-Can't do everything.

00:03:51.200 --> 00:03:53.968
-We're lucky to get
to do these things.

00:03:53.968 --> 00:03:56.000
So, anyways, we recorded
a song and a video.

00:03:56.000 --> 00:03:58.000
It's called
"It Was A...(Masked Christmas)."

00:03:58.000 --> 00:03:59.601
Ariana Grande,

00:03:59.601 --> 00:04:00.901
Megan Thee Stallion.

00:04:00.901 --> 00:04:02.868
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:04:02.868 --> 00:04:04.834
It drops tonight.

00:04:04.834 --> 00:04:06.501
It drops tonight at midnight.

00:04:06.501 --> 00:04:08.934
[ Cheering intensifies ]
-Whoa!
-So it's out tonight!

00:04:08.934 --> 00:04:12.901
I'm freaking out!
Like this is major.

00:04:12.901 --> 00:04:15.501
Like I'm seriously, really
seriously reacting to this

00:04:15.501 --> 00:04:17.200
